**Theorem 7.2 (strict correction to optimal individual local constants).**
Definition 7.1 has exactly the $2^n$ actual tuples
$x_i=\langle s_i,s_{i+1}\rangle$, each with one seed lift, and
prescribed incidence two. Its exact mass is

$$
Z_n=\frac{3^n+1}{6^n}.
\tag{OOA.27}
$$

Each individual local COK minimax constant is exactly
$c=\sqrt{10}/6$. Choose the credited binary rows

$$
Q_\varnothing(a)=\tfrac12,\qquad
Q_{\{i+1\}}(a\mid b)=
\begin{cases}4/5,&a=b,\\1/5,&a\ne b.\end{cases}
\tag{OOA.28}
$$

For every edge, every preceding subset and every full context, its
two-order affinity is exactly $3/\sqrt{10}<1$. If $4\mid n$, then

$$
Z_n\le
\left[\frac{\sqrt{10}}6
 \left(\frac{1+3/\sqrt{10}}2\right)^{1/4}\right]^n
<\left(\frac{\sqrt{10}}6\right)^n.
\tag{OOA.29}
$$

This is an extensive correction to the optimal individual local product
bound for these actual networks.

Proof. The root is branch, and its two immediate child factors force
the two actual leaves. All deeper prescribed factors are exactly theirs.
Conversely each binary seed assignment reconstructs these blocks and
satisfies every target equation. The actual left reply recovers $s_i$,
proving uniqueness and the count. Each seed occurs in its owner and
its predecessor block. The mass is the cyclic matrix sum
$6^{-n}\operatorname{tr}\bigl((\begin{smallmatrix}2&1\\1&2\end{smallmatrix})^n\bigr)$;
its eigenvalues $3,1$ prove (OOA.27). This transfer matrix represents
only this explicitly realized subfamily.

There is one incoming owner per block, so the two COK coefficients are
$1/2$. For equal or unequal leaves, respectively, direct substitution
gives

$$
\Phi_i^2=\frac{10}{36}\,Q_\varnothing(s_i)
                              Q_{\{i+1\}}(s_i\mid s_{i+1}).
\tag{OOA.30}
$$

Thus the pointwise local bound with $c$ is equality. To see optimality,
use on the four local inputs the single law assigning $2/5$ to each
equal input and $1/10$ to each unequal input. Its owned marginal and
conditional rows are exactly (OOA.28). Taking logs in (OOA.30) and
expectations under this law makes the local entropy functional equal
to $\log_2c$. Conditional relative entropy then forces every other
positive-kernel local cap to be at least $c$. This is the finite
minimax mechanism of [COK, Theorem 4.1][COK], with all four inputs
in its support-aware relation. COK §8 owns the two-block calculation
and these binary weights and rows; the cyclic joint correction is the
additional conclusion here.

For edge $i,i+1$, orient it in that order. Let $p(b)$ be the second
endpoint's row, conditioned on $s_{i+2}$ if that owner is earlier,
and uniform otherwise. In either order it is the same $p$. The two
paired rows are $\tfrac12p(b)$ and
$p(b)Q_{\{i+1\}}(a\mid b)$. Their affinity is

$$
\sum_bp(b)\left(\sqrt{2/5}+\sqrt{1/10}\right)
=\frac3{\sqrt{10}},
\tag{OOA.31}
$$

independently of that full context. The predecessor of $i$ is irrelevant
to these rows. The dependency graph is the actual undirected cycle,
and each $W_e$ has four vertices. For $n=4k$, select edges
$(4r,4r+1)$, $0\le r<k$, with indices modulo $n$. Their neighborhoods
$\{4r-1,4r,4r+1,4r+2\}$ partition the cycle. Apply Theorem 5.1 with
$\delta_e=1-3/\sqrt{10}$ to obtain (OOA.29). $\square$

